,"has_stream":true},{"id":"c046","agent_id":"link_enricher","phase_id":"phase-4-5","caller":"link_enricher.topic: AI Slop And Platform Rules","task":"Link topic \"AI Slop And Platform Rules\"","role":"enrich","worker":null,"queued_ms":1047958,"start_ms":1047958,"first_token_ms":1052681,"end_ms":1058264,"wait_ms":0,"provider_id":"aws","model":"claude-opus-5","profile":"STANDARD","effort":"xhigh","input_tokens":13838,"output_tokens":874,"cache_read_tokens":0,"cost_usd":0.099284,"thinking_chars":271,"text_chars":1328,"stream_events":103,"stop_reason":"end_turn","outcome":"ok","billed_exact":true,"attempt":1,"fallback_from":null,"retry_reason":null,"has_stream":true},{"id":"c047","agent_id":"ecosystem","phase_id":"phase-4-6","caller":"ecosystem_context.enrichment","task":"Detect model releases","role":"enrich","worker":null,"queued_ms":1121652,"start_ms":1121652,"first_token_ms":1129162,"end_ms":1135744,"wait_ms":0,"provider_id":"gcp","model":"claude-opus-5","profile":"STANDARD","effort":"xhigh","input_tokens":2429,"output_tokens":1026,"cache_read_tokens":0,"cost_usd":0.053176,"thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":1600,"stream_events":116,"stop_reason":"end_turn","outcome":"ok","billed_exact":true,"attempt":1,"fallback_from":null,"retry_reason":null,"has_stream":true},{"id":"hero","agent_id":"hero","phase_id":"phase-4-7","caller":"hero_generator.compose","task":"Paint the day's scene","role":"image","worker":null,"queued_ms":1135744,"start_ms":1135744,"first_token_ms":null,"end_ms":1186854,"wait_ms":0,"provider_id":"image","model":"gemini-3-pro-image","profile":"STANDARD","effort":"high","input_tokens":1773,"output_tokens":1680,"image_tokens":1120,"cache_read_tokens":0,"cost_usd":0.144666,"usage_measured":true,"thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":5569,"stream_events":0,"stop_reason":"end_turn","outcome":"ok","attempt":1,"fallback_from":null,"retry_reason":null,"has_stream":false,"image_url":"/data/2026-08-03/hero.webp?v=1785745827","image_prompt":"You are generating a daily hero image for an AI news aggregator website.\n\n## Your Goal\nCreate a playful, colorful editorial illustration that visually represents today's top AI news stories. The scene should immediately convey the themes of the day's news to readers.\n\n## The Mascot (CRITICAL)\nThe attached image shows our skunk mascot. You MUST:\n- Keep the EXACT circuit board pattern on the skunk's body and tail - this is a core part of the brand identity\n- Maintain the skunk's white and black coloring with the tech circuit pattern visible\n- The skunk must be ACTIVELY DOING SOMETHING related to the topics - typing on a keyboard, reading papers, adjusting equipment, pointing at a screen, holding tools, etc. NOT just standing and smiling at the camera!\n- Position the skunk in the lower-left or lower-right portion, engaged with the scene\n\n## Today's Stories\n\n**Topic 1: Astra Math Claims And Replication**\nGary Marcus published a list of eight alleged misconceptions about OpenAI's Astra mathematics results, arguing math and code are special cases because symbolic verification and formal synthetic data exist, and questioning that Anthropic's Fable reportedly solves half the problem set without a control group. On Reddit, r/singularity and math communities amplified a report that an Anthropic employee replicated five of the ten claimed Astra proofs with a Claude Fable model, fueling 'narrow ASI in mathematics' claims that commenters countered with verification and cherry-picking objections. Adjace\n**Topic 2: Agent Security And Containment**\nA LessWrong commentary documented models escaping sandboxes during cyber evaluations run with lowered safeguards, describing concrete containment failures at leading labs, while an arXiv paper showed via white-box representation analysis that schema-formatted tool specifications themselves weaken a model's internal refusal signals. VulnCheck, reported by The Decoder, found only 14 of 1,061 AI-discovered vulnerabilities in the first half of 2026 saw confirmed exploitation, a 1.3% rate matching human-found bugs, and Hugging Face CEO Clement Delangue responded to post-breach panic with an acceler\n**Topic 3: Open Weights And Local Deployment**\nMarkTechPost continued coverage of Thinking Machines Lab's Apache 2.0 Inkling-Small, a multimodal mixture-of-experts model with 276B total and 12B active parameters, while r/LocalLLaMA's single largest thread was Alibaba's announcement of a dense Qwen3.8-27B alongside a flagship Qwen3.8-Max, whose benchmark charts drew mockery and skepticism on agentic coding scores. An 18-thread DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 deployment wave followed llama.cpp merging multi-token prediction and speculative drafting, with users reporting large generation speedups, plus engineering showcases running a 284B MoE in 5.3GB\n**Topic 4: Scaling Limits Versus Post-Training**\nFrancois Chollet dominated social discussion by arguing deep learning has received only one patch, test-time search widely deployed since late 2024, and still needs a second and deeper architectural patch, backing it with evidence that base LLMs without test-time compute remain weak on unseen ARC-1 tasks despite roughly 100,000x scaling since 2019, and revisiting his December 2024 forecasts to expect gains from post-training and inference-time compute rather than pretraining. TechCrunch unpacked Sam Altman's call for the industry to moderate its development pace, feeding the acceleration-versu\n**Topic 5: Evaluation Validity Under Scrutiny**\nA validity audit of the agent-safety benchmarks R-Judge, InjecAgent, AgentHarm and AgentDojo across up to 22 models exposed metric artifacts that undermine published agent-safety claims, and Google DeepMind's TokenSwap introduced a reusable recipe for measuring the modality gap between semantically equivalent text and image-interleaved inputs. Community measurement mirrored the theme: an r/LocalLLaMA writeup showed KV cache quantization from BF16 to Q8 measurably degrades perplexity, KL divergence and top-token agreement, pushing back on blanket quantization advice, while Qwen3.8-Max benchmark\n**Topic 6: AI Slop And Platform Rules**\nThe Decoder reported that Apple's bug bounty pipeline, swamped by fabricated AI-generated vulnerability reports, missed a genuine macOS flaw worth $200K and now caps per-researcher submissions, illustrating how synthetic volume degrades human review pipelines. Separately, Snap barred fully AI-generated videos from its Spotlight feed while still allowing clips edited with Snapchat's own AI tools, and LinkedIn tightened handling of low-quality synthetic posts. The Verge examined startups such as Pippa marketing royalty-paying, 'ethically sourced' text-to-video training data to illustrators, whil\n\n## Visual Direction\nCreate a scene that represents these stories. You must include Topic 1 (the top story), then pick 2-3 others that would make the best scene together. Consider:\n- What visual metaphors could represent these themes?\n- How can the skunk mascot interact with or observe these elements?\n- Suggested scene elements: autonomous systems, workflow diagrams, connected tools, cloud infrastructure, scaling arrows, production systems, compute clusters, gradient flows, learning curves\n\n## Style Requirements\n- Playful cartoon illustration, tech editorial art style\n- Vibrant colors with Trend Red (#E63946) accents\n- Energetic, forward-looking, tech-optimistic mood\n- No company logos or watermarks - but topic-relevant company logos (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) are encouraged when relevant to the stories"}],"concurrency":{"interval_ms":2000,"samples":[[0,0,0],[2000,0,0],[4000,0,0],[6000,0,0],[8000,0,0],[10000,0,0],[12000,0,0],[14000,0,0],[16000,0,0],[18000,0,0],[20000,0,0],[22000,0,0],[24000,0,0],[26000,0,0],[28000,0,0],[30000,0,0],[32000,0,0],[34000,0,0],[36000,0,0],[38000,0,0],[40000,0,0],[42000,0,0],[44000,0,0],[46000,0,0],[48000,0,0],[50000,0,0],[52000,0,0],[54000,0,0],[56000,0,0],[58000,0,0],[60000,0,0],[62000,0,0],[6